 "lead_paragraphs": [
  {
   "label": {
    "en": "CAPITAL RETURNS:",
    "zh": "现金分配："
   },
   "text": {
    "en": "FY12-25 OCF $50.8B less capex $10.4B left **$40.4B FCF**. Buybacks **$19.7B (49%)**; dividends **$15.8B (39%)**; acquisitions **$11.2B** (CSRA ~$10B in 2018, debt paid down since).",
    "zh": "FY12-25 OCF $50.8B 减资本开支 $10.4B，得 **FCF $40.4B**。回购 **$19.7B（49%）**；股息 **$15.8B（39%）**；收购 **$11.2B**（2018 年 CSRA，其后逐步还债）。"
   }
  },
  {
   "label": {
    "en": "NET SHARES:",
    "zh": "净股数变化："
   },
   "text": {
    "en": "Diluted shares FY11 368M to FY25 272M, **down 26%** (about 2.1% a year). Buybacks slowed after FY24 as cash went to debt repayment and submarine capacity.",
    "zh": "稀释股数由 FY11 的 368M 降至 FY25 的 272M，**减少 26%**（每年约 2.1%）。FY24 后回购放缓，现金更多用于还债和潜艇产能。"
   }
  }
 ],
 "commentary": [
  {
   "headline": {
    "en": "Growth came back after a flat decade.",
    "zh": "沉寂十年后增长回来了。"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Revenue was flat at ~$31B in FY11-17, then rose to $52.6B by FY25 (+10.1% in FY25) on Gulfstream's new jets and submarine demand. Q3 2026 revenue was $14.6B.",
    "zh": "FY11-17 营收持平在约 $310 亿，之后在湾流新机型和潜艇需求带动下增至 FY25 的 $526 亿（FY25 +10.1%）。2026年Q3 营收 $146 亿。"
   }
  },
  {
   "headline": {
    "en": "Submarines bring volume, not margin.",
    "zh": "潜艇带来规模，不带来利润率。"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Marine is the largest segment (32%) but earns only 7.0%. Columbia- and Virginia-class ramp-ups keep margins low for now; my model lets them rise to 8.5% by 2028.",
    "zh": "海事是最大的分部（32%），但利润率只有 7.0%。哥伦比亚级和弗吉尼亚级潜艇扩产使利润率暂时偏低；我的模型让它在 2028 年升至 8.5%。"
   }
  },
  {
   "headline": {
    "en": "Gulfstream is the margin engine.",
    "zh": "湾流是利润引擎。"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Aerospace grew 16.5% in FY25 to $13.1B at a 13.3% margin as G700 and G800 deliveries ramped; I take it to 15% by 2028. Business-jet demand is the most cyclical part of the group, so a downturn would hit the highest-margin segment first.",
    "zh": "随着 G700 和 G800 交付提速，航空航天 FY25 增长 16.5% 至 $131 亿，利润率 13.3%；我假设 2028 年达到 15%。公务机需求是公司最具周期性的部分，经济下行时利润率最高的分部会最先受到冲击。"
   }
  },
  {
   "headline": {
    "en": "Cash returns are steady.",
    "zh": "现金分配稳定。"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "FCF has been $1.8-4.0B a year for over a decade and almost all of it was returned: buybacks 49% and dividends 39% of FY12-25 FCF. Net debt/EBITDA fell to 1.2x after the CSRA deal.",
    "zh": "十多年来 FCF 每年 $18-40 亿，几乎全部返还给股东：FY12-25 回购占 FCF 49%、股息占 39%。收购 CSRA 后净债务/EBITDA 已降至 1.2 倍。"
   }
  },
  {
   "headline": {
    "en": "The backlog gives visibility.",
    "zh": "积压订单提供了可见度。"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "A $220B backlog covers more than four years of revenue, and defence orders ran at 8.5x book-to-bill in Q3. The risk is execution and budget timing, not demand: shipyard labour and supplier delays have slowed submarine deliveries before.",
    "zh": "$2,200 亿积压订单覆盖四年以上的营收，Q3 国防订单出货比达 8.5 倍。风险在于执行和预算时点，而不是需求：船厂人手和供应商延误过去就曾拖慢潜艇交付。"
   }
  },
  {
   "headline": {
    "en": "My DCF is below Morningstar.",
    "zh": "我的 DCF 低于 Morningstar。"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Base $342.81 (WACC 8.2%, g 2.5%, beta 0.75) needs $70.4B revenue by 2030 (6.0% a year) at a 10.9% EBIT margin; TV is 81% of EV. At $359.69 that is -5%. Morningstar ($438) uses a 7.9% WACC and an 11.7% margin.",
    "zh": "基准价值 $342.81（WACC 8.2%，g 2.5%，beta 0.75）要求 2030 年营收 $704 亿（年增 6.0%）、EBIT 利润率 10.9%；终值占 EV 81%。按 $359.69 计为 -5%。Morningstar（$438）用 7.9% 的 WACC 和 11.7% 的利润率。"
   }
  }
 ],
